# No em dashes in UI copy

Do **not** use the em dash (`—`) or en dash (`–`) anywhere in user-facing text for DiffuseCut.

This includes JSX text, labels, placeholders, tooltips, badges, error messages, empty states, preset descriptions, and any string shown in the browser.

## Use instead

- Comma: `Live-action look, casting-style references`
- Colon: `Your own look: add a style phrase`
- Period: two short sentences
- Parentheses: `API key (OpenAI) (saved)`

## Examples

```tsx
// BAD
description: "Live-action look — casting-style references"
{saved ? " — saved" : ""}

// GOOD
description: "Live-action look, casting-style references"
{saved ? " (saved)" : ""}
```

## Scope

- **Enforce** in `src/app/`, `src/components/`, and UI strings in `src/lib/` (e.g. preset labels).
- Code comments and internal logs are lower priority, but prefer avoiding dashes there too when touching the file.

Before finishing UI work, search changed files for `—` and `–` and remove them.
